Important SSH Client Configuration
~/.ssh/config

Common directives:

Directive	   Purpose
Host	        Alias used with ssh
HostName	    Actual server hostname/IP
User	        Remote username
Port	        SSH port
IdentityFile	Private key to use

Host webserver
    HostName 192.168.1.100
    User student
    Port 22
    IdentityFile ~/.ssh/id_ed25519


# vi ~/.ssh/config


Host servera
    HostName servera.example.com
    User usera
    IdentityFile ~/.ssh/id_rsa_servera

Host serverb
    HostName serverb.example.com
    User userb
    IdentityFile ~/.ssh/id_rsa_serverb


Now you can simply type:
# ssh servera

instead of:
# ssh -i ~/.ssh/id_rsa_servera usera@servera.example.com

And:
# ssh serverb

instead of:
# ssh -i ~/.ssh/id_rsa_serverb userb@serverb.example.com



Direct Key vs ssh-agent
=============================
Without agent
#ssh -i .ssh/key-with-pass user@remotehost

SSH directly uses that private key.

With agent
#eval $(ssh-agent)
#ssh-add .ssh/key-with-pass

#ssh-add -l
#ssh user@remotehost

The agent provides the key when SSH needs it.

Remember
ssh-keygen
     │
     ▼
Creates keys

ssh-add
     │
     ▼
Loads private key into ssh-agent

ssh
     │
     ▼
Uses key for authentication



| Command                   | Purpose                                         |
| ------------------------- | ----------------------------------------------- |
| `ssh user@host`           | Connect to remote host                          |
| `ssh host`                | Connect using client configuration/default user |
| `ssh user@host hostname`  | Run remote command                              |
| `ssh-keygen`              | Generate SSH key pair                           |
| `ssh-keygen -lf file.pub` | Display key fingerprint                         |
| `ssh-keygen -R host`      | Remove host from `known_hosts`                  |
| `ssh-copy-id user@host`   | Copy public key to server                       |
| `ssh-add key`             | Add private key to ssh-agent                    |
| `ssh-add -l`              | List keys in agent                              |
| `ssh -i key user@host`    | Use a specific private key                      |
| `ssh -v user@host`        | Verbose troubleshooting                         |
| `cat ~/.ssh/known_hosts`  | View user's known hosts                         |
| `cat ~/.ssh/config`       | View SSH client configuration                   |
| `sshd -t`                 | Validate SSH server configuration               |
| `systemctl reload sshd`   | Reload SSH server configuration                 |
| `systemctl status sshd`   | Check SSH server status                         |





